 "scope_note": "A construction check on the reference chart. It does not measure the actual universe. Finding no signature at the cut is a statement about this chart; it does not show that the parent/child boundary is unreal in any construction, only that this one carries nothing there.",
 "what_this_measures": "Whether the parent/child cut carries any signature at all. Every quantity the chart carries is tested for a local feature there, against a threshold scaled by the chart's own total variation, so a smooth function does not read as structure.",
 "why_it_matters": "The construction nests a parent and a child, and the only physical interface it contains is at r_plus, below the child rather than at its boundary. If the cut carries nothing, the nesting is bookkeeping. If it carries something, that is the boundary condition the nesting is missing."
